  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/2dcb5ff4-85e4-492f-b1e4-31a14c01f623-image.png\" style=\"width: 446px; height: 199px;\" /></p><p>This structure represents sucrose in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo></math>glucose and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo></math>fructose is attached to each other by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> glycosidic linkage. Since reducing groups of glucose and fructose are involved in glycosidic bond formation, this is considered as non-reducing sugar.</p>",
    "image": null
